# Core Standards

## TypeScript
- Strict mode throughout — `tsconfig.json` must have `"strict": true`
- Never use `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow it explicitly
- Use `interface` for all type definitions, not `type` aliases

## Components
- Functional components only — no class components

## Control Flow
- Guard clauses for early returns instead of nested `if` statements

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
function process(user: User | null) {
  if (user) {
    if (user.isActive) {
      doWork(user);
    }
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD
function process(user: User | null) {
  if (!user) return;
  if (!user.isActive) return;
  doWork(user);
}
```

## Naming
- Descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs: `isLoading`, `hasError`, `canSubmit`

## Logging
- Never use `console.log` in production code — use a logger service instead

## Error Handling
- Always handle errors explicitly — no empty catch blocks, no silent failures
